  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Magnesium aspartate is a magnesium salt used as a mineral supplement to treat or prevent magnesium deficiency. It is listed as an investigational drug and is not an approved medicine in the European Union; it is mainly available as a dietary supplement.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q72488024&quot;>Wikidata Q72488024</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>magnesium aspartate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A12CC05</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13359&quot;>DB13359</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q72488024&quot;>Q72488024</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C8H20MgN2O12</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>360.555 g/mol (Drugs.Common (25.09))</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
end MagnesiumAspartate;
